- Compared the reset lifecycle with pinned Java 5.5.1 source at `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`: `MQClientInstance.resetOffset`, `waitResetOffsetReady`, and `RebalancePushImpl.removeUnnecessaryMessageQueue` / `tryRemoveOrderMessageQueue`.
- Updated Rust reset handling to select only live process queues represented in the input table; drop and clear matching queues even for null offsets; wait Java's 10-second non-orderly drain or orderly consume-lock window; write only non-null offsets; then perform the Java 500-ms orderly removal attempt. A timed-out orderly removal still removes the local queue but leaves the offset-store entry; successful removal persists, removes the stored offset and unlocks. Reset values are not frozen, and generation fencing rejects late work. The process-queue unlock delay now begins at queue creation.
